  "meta": {
    "name": "Tally design tokens",
    "task": "M0.5-03",
    "status": "owner-approved 2026-11-18 (M0.5-O1, issue #15 comment 6991804241); T2 decided 2026-11-18: keep the Material 3 type scale and always follow the system font scale, issue #15 comment 6991847257. T1 decided: Petrol palette (owner, 2026-11-17, issue #15 comment 6956773225)",
    "units": "spacing, size and shape in integer dp; type size and line height in integer sp; colors as #RRGGBB",
    "font": "Roboto (Android system default, no bundled font)",
    "notes": "Material 3 roles. Theme.kt is written by hand from this file; M1-04 tests parity and WCAG AA contrast of contrastPairs. Colors are Material roles only, so tokens stay theme-swappable: a user-chosen app theme (post-v1, docs/product/stories.md) replaces the whole light and dark color sets, and no code or page may hard-code a palette value. Every Material 3 ColorScheme role is defined (scripts/design_tokens.py REQUIRED_ROLES); background, onBackground, surfaceTint, surfaceBright (light) and surfaceDim (dark) alias existing roles, the Fixed roles reuse the tone 10/30/80/90 values of the secondary, tertiary and primary palettes, and surfaceVariant, surfaceDim (light) and surfaceBright (dark) are tones of the neutral palettes."
  },
